"What to Bring When Applying – Provisional (https://www.dps.texas.gov/Internetforms/Forms/DL-68.pdf)\nciteturn26view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 3; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dps.texas.gov/Internetforms/Forms/DL-68.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 147\nL0@P0: What to bring with you when you are applying\nL1@P0: as a Teen Driver for your Provisional Driver License\nL2@P0: There are two phases you will need to complete before graduating to a full driver license. This is called the\nL3@P0: Graduated Driver License Program for teens. To be issued a provisional driver license (phase II) in the\nL4@P0: state of Texas, you must bring the following documentation to your local driver license office:\nL5@P0: 1. Application for a Provisional Texas Driver License\nL6@P0: 2. Proof of Identity (Your Texas Learner License is sufficient)\nL7@P0: 3. Evidence of Lawful Status (If you are not a U.S. Citizen)\nL8@P0: 4. Provide Social Security Number\nL9@P0: 5. Proof of Completion for an Impact Texas Driver (ITD) course\nL10@P0: 6. Proof of Completion for Driver Education\nL11@P0: 7. Proof of Insurance (if you will be taking a driving test)\nL12@P0: 8. Issuance Fee\nL13@P0: This checklist will help you identify what documents in each section you will need to bring to your local driver\nL14@P0: license office so that you may obtain your provisional DL. Follow the directions listed for each section, and\nL15@P0: check the appropriate document(s) you have that you can bring with you.\nL16@P0: To start the application process, first complete all sections and collect your documents. All visits to the driver\nL17@P0: license office are by appointment only and require your and a parent or legal guardian to be present. Visit\nL18@P0: https://public.txdpsscheduler.com/ to schedule an appointment.\nL19@P0: Section 1. Proof of Identity\nL20@P0: A. Acceptable Identification Document List. Documents must be original or a copy certified by the issuing\nL21@P0: agency. No photocopies are accepted.\nL22@P0: Check one document you have from this section. This will be your proof of identity.\nL23@P0: ☐ Texas DL or ID within two years of expiration ☐ Unexpired US passport book or passport card\nL24@P0: ☐ US Citizenship Certificate or Certificate of\nL25@P0: Naturalization with identifiable photo (N-550, N\u0002560, N-561, N-570, or N-578)\nL26@P0: ☐ Unexpired US military photo ID card for active\nL27@P0: duty, reserve, or retired personnel\nL28@P0: ☐ Unexpired Foreign passport, visa* (Visa may be valid or expired), and I-94\nL29@P0: Unexpired Department of Homeland Security (DHS) or United States Citizenship and Immigration Services\nL30@P0: (USCIS) photo ID. Examples include:\nL31@P0: ☐ US citizen Identification card (I-179 or I-197) ☐ Permanent Resident card (I-551)\nL32@P0: ☐ Machine-Readable Immigrant Visa (MRIV) with\nL33@P0: temporary I-551 language and Alien Documentation,\nL34@P0: Identification and Telecommunications System\nL35@P0: (ADIT) stamp\nL36@P0: ☐ Employment Authorization card “EAD” (I-766)\nL37@P0: ☐ Advance parole document with photo (I-512 or I-512L)\nL38@P0: ☐ I-94 stamped “Sec. 208 Asylee” with photo ☐ I-94 stamped “Sec. 207 Refugee” with photo\nL39@P0: ☐ Valid refugee travel letter with photo and stamped\nL40@P0: by US Customs and Border Protection (CBP)\nL41@P0: ☐ Northern Mariana card (I-873)\nL42@P0: ☐ American Indian card (I-872)\nL43@P0: ☐ A birth certificate or birth record issued by the appropriate State Bureau of Vital Statistics or equivalent\nL44@P0: agency from a US state or local government, a US territory, the District of Columbia, or a Canadian\nL45@P0: province\nL46@P0: ☐ For U.S. citizens born abroad, a certificate of Report of Birth (DS-1350 or FS-545) or Consular Report of\nL47@P0: Birth (FS-240) issued by the U.S. Department of State\nL48@P0: ☐ A court order with name and date of birth indicating an official change of name and/or gender from a US\nL49@P0: state, a US territory, the District of Columbia, or a Canadian province\nL50@P0-1: DL-68 (Rev. 10-2025) ☐ Temporary receipt for a Texas DL or ID (actual\nL51@P1: receipt)\nL52@P1: ☐ Expired Texas DL or ID (expired more than two\nL53@P1: years—actual card)\nL54@P1: ☐ DL or ID issued by another US state, US territory,\nL55@P1: District of Columbia, or Canadian province\nL56@P1: (unexpired or within two years of the expiration\nL57@P1: date – actual card)*\nL58@P1: ☐ Original or certified copy of a marriage\nL59@P1: certificate or divorce decree (US jurisdiction or\nL60@P1: foreign jurisdiction-if not in English, a certified\nL61@P1: translation must accompany it)\nL62@P1: ☐ Pilot’s license (actual card)* ☐ Concealed handgun license or License to Carry\nL63@P1: (actual card)*\nL64@P1: ☐ Unexpired US military dependent ID card (actual\nL65@P1: card)\nL66@P1: ☐ Professional license issued by Texas state\nL67@P1: agency\nL68@P1: ☐ Veteran’s ID or Health Identification card “VHIC”\nL69@P1: (actual card)\nL70@P1: ☐ School records (e.g. report cards, photo ID\nL71@P1: cards, etc.)*\nL72@P1: ☐ Voter registration card (actual card)* ☐ Military records (e.g., Form DD-214)\nL73@P1: ☐ W-2 or 1099 form ☐ Selective Service card (actual card)\nL74@P1: ☐ Current Texas motor vehicle registration or title\nL75@P1: (TRC 521.144)\nL76@P1: ☐ Any insurance policy (valid continuously for the\nL77@P1: past two years)\nL78@P1: ☐ ID card issued by government agency* ☐ Current Texas boat registration or title\nL79@P1: ☐ Hospital-issued birth record* ☐ Medicare or Medicaid card (actual card)\nL80@P1: ☐ Immunization records* ☐ Unexpired foreign passport\nL81@P1: ☐ A valid Consular document issued by a state or\nL82@P1: national government\nL83@P1: ☐ Tribal membership card from a federally\nL84@P1: recognized tribe\nL85@P1: ☐ Texas Department of Criminal Justice (TDCJ)\nL86@P1: parole or mandatory release certificate\nL87@P1: ☐ Texas inmate ID card or similar form of ID\nL88@P1: issued by TDCJ\nL89@P1: ☐ Federal inmate ID card ☐ Federal parole or release certificate\nL90@P1: ☐ Certificate of Degree of Indian Blood (CDIB) ☐ Social Security card (actual card)\nL91@P1: *Document must be issued by an institution, entity or government agency from a US state, a US territory, the District of Columbia, or a\nL92@P1: Canadian province.\nL93@P1: .\nL94@P1: Section 2. Proof of U.S. Citizenship or Lawful Presence\nL95@P1: If you are a United States Citizen and have already presented this documentation to the Department, you may skip\nL96@P1: this section and proceed to Section 3. If you have a Limited-Term Texas driver license, you will be required to\nL97@P1: present updated evidence of lawful presence. Most documents will be verified through the US Department of\nL98@P1: Homeland Security’s SAVE Program. Verification through SAVE is often instantaneous, but when it is not, receipt of\nL99@P1: the DL/ID may be delayed for up to 30 days.\nL100@P1: Check one document you have from this list that contains your full legal name. This will be your proof of\nL101@P1: U.S. Citizenship or Lawful Presence in the United States.\nL102@P1: ☐ Birth certificate or birth record issued by the appropriate State Bureau of Vital Statistics or equivalent agency\nL103@P1: from a US state or local government, a US territory, or the District of Columbia\nL104@P1: ☐ US Passport Book or Passport card ☐ US Citizen Identification card (I-179 or I-197)\nL105@P1: ☐ Permanent Resident card (I-551) ☐ I-94\nL106@P1: ☐ I-94 stamped “Sec. 208 Asylee” or “Sec. 207\nL107@P1: Refugee”\nL108@P1: ☐ US Travel Document (I-327 or I-571)\nL109@P1: ☐ Employment Authorization Card “EAD” (I-766) ☐ I-551 stamp in foreign passport\nL110@P1: ☐ US Department of State Certificate of Birth Abroad\nL111@P1: issued to US citizens born abroad (Form FS-240,\nL112@P1: DS-1350, or FS-545)\nL113@P1: ☐ US Citizenship Certificate or Certificate of\nL114@P1: Naturalization (N-550, N-560, N-561, N-570, or\nL115@P1: N-578)\nL116@P1: ☐ Machine Readable Immigrant Visa with temporary\nL117@P1: I-551 language and ADIT stamp\nL118@P1: ☐ Student documents with Student Exchange and\nL119@P1: Visitor Information System (SEVIS) number\nL120@P1: ☐ I-20 Non-immigrant students (F-1) ☐ DS-2019 Exchange Visitor (J-1) certificate\nL121@P1-2: ☐ Non-student documents with alien number or I-94 numberSection 3. Proof of Impact Texas Driver (ITD) Course completion and Driving Test\nL122@P2: You must have successfully completed an ITD program within 90 days of taking your driving test. Select one:\nL123@P2: ☐ I have completed the ITD Course and driving test at a Certified Driver Training School and will be\nL124@P2: bringing the driving test results to the driver license office in a sealed, unaltered envelope\nL125@P2: ☐ I have completed the ITD Course and driving test through a Public School Driver Education Program and\nL126@P2: will be bringing the driving test results to the driver license office in a sealed, unaltered envelope\nL127@P2: ☐ I have completed the ITD course within the previous 90 days and will be taking the driving test at my local\nL128@P2: driver license office. I will be bringing my ITD Course completion Certificate.\nL129@P2: Section 5. Driver Education\nL130@P2: You must provide a certificate of completion from your course provider for both the classroom and behind-the-wheel\nL131@P2: portions of driver education. Select one:\nL132@P2: ☐ Commercial Driver Training School (Form DE-964/DEE-964)\nL133@P2: ☐ Parent Taught Driver Education (Form DE-964/DEE-964)\nL134@P2: ☐ Public School Driver Education (DE-964E)\nL135@P2: Section 6. Proof of Insurance\nL136@P2: If you have not taken the driving skills exam during driver education, you will be required to successfully pass the\nL137@P2: drive test at your local driver license office. Once you have completed all of the requirements on this checklist, you\nL138@P2: may schedule your drive test at https://txdpsscheduler.com/\nL139@P2: ☐ Proof of Insurance (for the vehicle you will be using for the driving skills exam, if applicable)\nL140@P2: Upon completing all sections, gather the documents you have checked and bring them to your local driver\nL141@P2: license office to begin the renewal process.\nL142@P2: Section 4. Provide Social Security Number\nL143@P2: You must provide your social security number. If the number is not already part of your driver record, the\nL144@P2: Department will verify SSN number electronically with the Social Security Administration (SSA). If the SSN cannot\nL145@P2: be verified, the Department will be unable to issue your Provisional License and additional instructions will be\nL146@P2: provided.\n"
